 "how_to_recognise_each_stage": {
  "tensioned": "the ropes come taut (HUD load cells, 0.5 s mean >= 20 N) and the platform has moved 5 cm from its start",
  "straight_tow": "the cargo centre reaches the x of the inner corner (the end of the first leg)",
  "corner": "the cargo centre reaches the y of the inner corner (the platform has turned into the second leg)",
  "in_goal": "the whole cargo (its real footprint and heading) is inside the green goal area",
  "released_settled": "the cargo has rested inside the goal for 2 s with every check true (towing stopped; the ropes may stay loaded)",
  "first_violation": "the first sample at which an evidence check fails: what happened physically at that moment",
  "end": "the last two seconds of an unsuccessful episode: where the cargo and the robots ended"
 },
 "checklist": {
  "1_no_reward_hacking": "The cargo and the platform move only while a taut rope or a robot body acts on them (no jump, no motion without a cause); a stage is not credited before the video shows it; in shortcut and exploit runs the score comes only from progress that is visible.",
  "2_task_really_completed": "At the end the whole cargo lies inside the green area on the platform deck (not tipped, not resting on a robot), both ropes still attached at both ends, both robots standing; the cargo is at rest for the last 2 s.",
  "3_no_physics_violation": "No robot, rope segment, platform or cargo passes into a wall or the floor; nothing is launched or floats; no robot tips over (45 degrees) or skates on loaded feet; the rope never pushes (it only pulls when straight)."
 },
 "instructions": "For every video: mark on the video the time at which each stage is visibly complete (how_to_recognise_each_stage) into stage_timeline_manual and compare it with stage_timeline_verifier (the keyframe sheet shows -1 s / 0 / +1 s around each verifier time; the HUD clock is the simulated time); answer the three questions of `checklist` with reasons and timestamps, paying attention to the alarm locations and the first violation; sign (reviewer, role, date, signed). Where human and automatic judgement disagree, record it in disagreements, fix predicates, thresholds or monitors with the author, and rerun this tool.",
